# Reader panel demonstration: nine choices exercise scroll and compact viewports.
@scene notes
panel notebook
"Field notebook, day fourteen. An unexpected envelope arrived at dusk, sealed with a familiar copper emblem. Its ink seemed to shift whenever I turned the page."
"Nine possible interpretations are written beneath the sketch. Which thread should we follow?"
* "Examine the envelope's faded postmark and weather-worn corners." -> ending_1
* "Compare the ink with the entries on the preceding pages." -> ending_2
* "Read the address beneath the folded paper with a lamp." -> ending_3
* "Investigate the unusual emblem stamped into the seal." -> ending_4
* "Consult the star charts tucked behind the notebook." -> ending_5
* "Listen for footsteps outside the abandoned station." -> ending_6
* "Follow the trail left by the courier through the garden." -> ending_7
* "Open the envelope carefully without disturbing its edges." -> ending_8
* "Put the message aside and sketch what has happened." -> ending_9

@scene ending_1
panel banner
"Dispatch 01: The message belongs in the evening archive. This illustrated banner is an authored panel image, independent of the story text and its reader settings."
panel default
"The journal closes. The original solid panel returns without a restart."

